%[text] %[text:anchor:H_C875D022] ## How to interact with this live script 
%[text] All you have to do is read through everything and follow the outlined steps. The only thing you need to learn first is how to run a code block. 
%[text] If you see a grey rectangle with code in it that looks something like this, you just need to Navigate to the **Live Editor** tab at the top of your MATLAB window and click the ![](text:image:682b) **Run Section** button. The code inside the block will run, and you should see an output appear below the block.
disp('Hello!') %[output:6ec68a77]
%[text]{"align":"center"} ![Screenshot of the toolstrip showing the Live Editor tab \> Section \> Run Section relationship. ](text:image:4760)
%[text] Alternatively, click inside the code block and hit **CTRL** + **ENTER** on your keyboard. 
%[text] If you want to get rid of the outputs that have printed and start fresh, go to the **View** tab and select ![clear live script](text:image:917b) **Clear all Output**. You can also right-click in the live script and find **Clear Output** (run from a section in the live script to clear just that section but leave other outputs), or **Clear All Output**.
%[text]{"align":"center"} ![A screenshot of the toolstrip showing the View \> Output \> Clear All Output relationship](text:image:777d)
%%
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_B0BE071E] ## What to do when you run into trouble 
%[text] If you run a code cell and get an error like this line of red code: 
%[text] ![In a code box: penguins = readtable(filename)\nRed output follows: Unrecognized function or variable name 'filename'. ](text:image:3bf4)
%[text] First, make sure you ran all the code blocks above the block you're on. Some of them depend on each other! Second, double check that your MATLAB path is correct and has both your current live script and any data you downloaded. These are the two most common culprits when you're working with these live scripts. If you have access to MATLAB Copilot, you will also see a button that says ![Explain Error button](text:image:29cc). If you click this button it will open a Copilot Chat window and offer an explanation like:
%[text]{"align":"center"} ![Screenshot from Copilot chat explaining that the likely error is that filename is not defined before use. ](text:image:1a62)
%[text] For more details on using generative AI to support your learning, you could check out [Learning Engineering with GenAI](https://www.mathworks.com/matlabcentral/fileexchange/183786-learning-engineering-with-genai).
%[text] If you are writing your own code and run into issues, MATLAB makes it really easy to debug code ([helpful resource](https://www.mathworks.com/help/matlab/matlab_prog/debugging-process-and-features.html)). For slightly more advanced information on debugging code in MATLAB, check out the **Debugging** section of this [module](https://www.mathworks.com/matlabcentral/fileexchange/115905-programming-structuring-code). 
%[text] ***Tip***: you can always copy and paste your error into a search browser, there is almost always a post explaining what that error means in MATLAB Central Answers.
